{
  "id": "functions-and-inverses",
  "title": "Functions and Inverse Functions",
  "term": 1,
  "summary": "One-to-one and many-to-one functions, finding and sketching inverses of linear, quadratic and exponential functions, restricting the domain, and the vertical and horizontal line tests.",
  "notes": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Functions"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A **function** gives exactly one output for each input. **Vertical line test**: a graph is a function if no vertical line cuts it more than once.",
        "A **one-to-one** function: each output comes from exactly one input (e.g. $y = 2x + 1$).",
        "A **many-to-one** function: different inputs can give the same output (e.g. $y = x^2$, since $f(2) = f(-2)$)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Inverse functions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The **inverse** $f^{-1}$ undoes $f$. To find it: swap $x$ and $y$, then make $y$ the subject. The graph of $f^{-1}$ is the **reflection of $f$ in the line $y = x$**. The domain of $f$ becomes the range of $f^{-1}$, and vice versa."
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 1: linear",
      "problem": "Find $f^{-1}$ if $f(x) = 3x - 6$.",
      "steps": [
        "$y = 3x - 6$; swap: $x = 3y - 6$",
        "$y = \\dfrac{x + 6}{3}$, so $f^{-1}(x) = \\dfrac{1}{3}x + 2$"
      ],
      "answer": "$f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{1}{3}x + 2$"
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 320 260' font-family='sans-serif' font-size='10'><rect width='320' height='260' fill='white'/><line x1='18' y1='18' x2='18' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='38.3' y1='18' x2='38.3' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='58.6' y1='18' x2='58.6' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='78.9' y1='18' x2='78.9' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='99.1' y1='18' x2='99.1' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='119.4' y1='18' x2='119.4' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='139.7' y1='18' x2='139.7' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='160' y1='18' x2='160' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='180.3' y1='18' x2='180.3' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='200.6' y1='18' x2='200.6' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='220.9' y1='18' x2='220.9' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='241.1' y1='18' x2='241.1' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='261.4' y1='18' x2='261.4' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='281.7' y1='18' x2='281.7' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='302' y1='18' x2='302' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='242' x2='302' y2='242' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='226' x2='302' y2='226' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='210' x2='302' y2='210' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='194' x2='302' y2='194' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='178' x2='302' y2='178' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='162' x2='302' y2='162' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='146' x2='302' y2='146' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='130' x2='302' y2='130' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='114' x2='302' y2='114' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='98' x2='302' y2='98' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='82' x2='302' y2='82' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='66' x2='302' y2='66' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='50' x2='302' y2='50' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='34' x2='302' y2='34' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='18' y1='18' x2='302' y2='18' stroke='#e6e6e6'/><line x1='12' y1='130' x2='310' y2='130' st